# HTTPResponse Patterns

## Use Pre-Built Helpers
Prefer the response helpers from `HTTPResponse.hpp` over constructing responses manually.

```cpp
// ✅ GOOD — intent is clear, no boilerplate
return responseOK();
return responseBadRequest();
return responseNotFound();
return responseInternalServerError();
return responseUnauthorizedBasicAuth("Admin Area");

// ❌ BAD — verbose and error-prone
HTTPResponse res("200 OK");
res.setHeader("Content-Type", "text/plain");
res.setBody("OK");
return res;
```

## Available Helpers
| Helper | Code |
|--------|------|
| `responseOK()` | 200 |
| `responseCreated()` | 201 |
| `responseNoContent()` | 204 |
| `responseBadRequest()` | 400 |
| `responseAuthRequired()` | 401 |
| `responseUnauthorizedBasicAuth(realm)` | 401 + WWW-Authenticate |
| `responseForbidden()` | 403 |
| `responseNotFound()` | 404 |
| `responseMethodNotAllowed()` | 405 |
| `responseConflict()` | 409 |
| `responseInternalServerError()` | 500 |

## When to Construct Manually
Only build a raw `HTTPResponse` when you need custom headers or a body:
```cpp
HTTPResponse res("200 OK");
res.setHeader("Content-Type", "application/json");
res.setHeader("Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "*");
res.setBody(R"({"users":[]})");
return res;
```

## Multiple Headers of the Same Key
Use `addHeader` (not `setHeader`) for headers that can repeat:
```cpp
res.addHeader("Set-Cookie", "session=abc; HttpOnly");
res.addHeader("Set-Cookie", "theme=dark");
```
